Here's a clear, structured explanation of conduction, convection, and radiation, designed in an interactive textbook format:

```html
<div class="heat-transfer-container">
  <!-- Introduction Card -->
  <div class="card intro-card">
    <h2>Heat Transfer: Three Fundamental Modes</h2>
    <p>Heat always flows from higher to lower temperature. The mechanisms differ in how energy moves through space/matter:</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Conduction Card -->
  <div class="card conduction-card">
    <h3>Conduction: Direct Contact Transfer</h3>
    <div class="content">
      <p>▶️ <strong>Mechanism</strong>: Molecular collisions in solids/liquids (no bulk movement)</p>
      <p>▶️ <strong>Medium Required</strong>: Physical contact between objects</p>
      <p>▶️ <strong>Example</strong>: Spoon heating in soup, ice melting in hand</p>
    </div>

    <div class="formula-card">
      <h4>Fourier's Law of Conduction</h4>
      <div class="katex-formula">q = -k \cdot A \cdot \frac{\Delta T}{d}</div>
      <div class="formula-explanation">
        <span class="var">q</span> = Heat transfer rate (W)<br>
        <span class="var">k</span> = Thermal conductivity (W/m·K)<br>
        <span class="var">A</span> = Cross-sectional area (m²)<br>
        <span class="var">\Delta T</span> = Temperature difference (K)<br>
        <span class="var">d</span> = Material thickness (m)
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Convection Card -->
  <div class="card convection-card">
    <h3>Convection: Fluid Motion Transfer</h3>
    <div class="content">
      <p>▶️ <strong>Mechanism</strong>: Bulk fluid movement carrying heat</p>
      <p>▶️ <strong>Types</strong>:<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• Natural (buoyancy-driven, e.g., rising steam)<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;• Forced (pump/fan-driven, e.g., AC systems)</p>
      <p>▶️ <strong>Example</strong>: Boiling water, wind cooling skin</p>
    </div>

    <div class="formula-card">
      <h4>Newton's Law of Cooling</h4>
      <div class="katex-formula">q = h \cdot A \cdot (T_s - T_\infty)</div>
      <div class="formula-explanation">
        <span class="var">h</span> = Convective heat transfer coefficient (W/m²·K)<br>
        <span class="var">T_s</span> = Surface temperature<br>
        <span class="var">T_\infty</span> = Fluid temperature
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Radiation Card -->
  <div class="card radiation-card">
    <h3>Radiation: Electromagnetic Wave Transfer</h3>
    <div class="content">
      <p>▶️ <strong>Mechanism</strong>: Photon emission/absorption (no medium needed)</p>
      <p>▶️ <strong>Unique Feature</strong>: Works in vacuum (e.g., solar energy)</p>
      <p>▶️ <strong>Example</strong>: Sun warming Earth, infrared heaters</p>
    </div>

    <div class="formula-card">
      <h4>Stefan-Boltzmann Law</h4>
      <div class="katex-formula">q = \epsilon \sigma A T^4</div>
      <div class="formula-explanation">
        <span class="var">\epsilon</span> = Emissivity (0–1)<br>
        <span class="var">\sigma</span> = Stefan-Boltzmann constant (5.67×10⁻⁸ W/m²·K⁴)<br>
        <span class="var">T</span> = Absolute temperature (K)
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Comparison Table Card -->
  <div class="card table-card">
    <h3>Key Differences at a Glance</h3>
    <table class="comparison-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Feature</th>
          <th>Conduction</th>
          <th>Convection</th>
          <th>Radiation</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Medium Required</td>
          <td>Solid/stationary fluid</td>
          <td>Fluid (liquid/gas)</td>
          <td>None (works in vacuum)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Heat Carrier</td>
          <td>Molecular vibrations</td>
          <td>Fluid motion</td>
          <td>Electromagnetic waves</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Temperature Dependency</td>
          <td>Linear with ΔT</td>
          <td>Linear with ΔT</td>
          <td>∝ T⁴ (highly nonlinear)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Speed</td>
          <td>Slow</td>
          <td>Medium</td>
          <td>Speed of light</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Visual Evidence</td>
          <td>No visible sign</td>
          <td>Observed fluid flow</td>
          <td>Visible/infrared light</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!-- Real-World Example Card -->
  <div class="card example-card">
    <h3>Integrated Example: Campfire Experience</h3>
    <div class="example-content">
      <p>🔥 <strong>Conduction</strong>: Metal skewer heats up <em>(direct contact with flames)</em></p>
      <p>💨 <strong>Convection</strong>: Hot air rises to warm your face <em>(fluid motion)</em></p>
      <p>☀️ <strong>Radiation</strong>: Skin feels heat from 2m away <em>(infrared waves)</em></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

